## FOUNDING STORY & HISTORY

 

## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

 

## The Origin — 1983

 

Swatch was created in 1983 as an answer to the quartz crisis that had

devastated the Swiss watch industry. Nicolas G. Hayek, the visionary founder

of Swatch Group, developed a radically new concept: a watch made of fewer

parts (51 components vs. hundreds in traditional watches), assembled by

automated machines, made entirely in Switzerland, yet sold at a price that

competed with cheap Asian imports. The first Swatch collection launched in

March 1983.

Note: Swatch ≠ Swatch Group, Swatch Group is the parent company and includes Swatch and many other brands including Breguet, Harry Winston, Blancpain, Glashütte, Jaquet Droz, OMEGA, Longines, Rado, Union Glashütte, Tissot, Balmain, Certina, Mido, Hamilton, Swatch, Flik Flak.

## Key Milestones

 

1983: Swatch launches with 12 original models and two product lines GENT & LADY.

1985: First Swatch Art Special with Kiki Picasso paves the way for the “world’s smallest canvas” and many impressive artistic collaborations.

1989: The Swatch Proteam is created.

1990: Swatch launches new product line: CHRONO.

1994: Swatch launches new product line: IRONY.

1997: Swatch launches new product line: SKIN.

1998: Swatch launches Internet Time.

2004: Swatch revives the Cabaret Voltaire in Zurich, the birthplace of the Dada movement in 1916. This art and literary movement is one that continues to inspire Swatch.

2004: Swatch with Bill Gates launch PAPARAZZI, the first smartwatch.

2010: Swatch launches new product line: NEW GENT.

2013: Swatch launches its signature movement: SISTEM51 at Baselworld. SISTEM51 is the world’s first automatic mechanical watch movement made of just 51 parts and whose production is entirely automated. The 51 parts are grouped into five pre-assembled modules including 1 screw that fixes the oscillating weight. It has a 90-hour power reserve and is 100% Swiss Made.

2019: Swatch moves into its new HQ in Biel which features a Drive-Thru store.

2019: Swatch launches Swatch Pay.

2019: Swatch launches new product line: BIG BOLD.

2021: Swatch expands its BIOCERAMIC material (first introduced in 2018) across key product lines. BIOCERAMIC combines zirconium oxide ceramic powder with a biosourced material derived from castor oil. Lightweight, scratch-resistant, durable and soft to the touch.

2022: Swatch launches the Bioceramic MoonSwatch Collection, the result of its collaboration with sister brand OMEGA. The collection is sold in-store and online in some countries and becomes an instant hit worldwide.

2023: Swatch launches new product line: SQUARE BIOCERAMIC.

2023: Swatch launches the Bioceramic Scuba Fifty Fathoms Collection, the results of its collaboration with Blancpain. The watches in this collection pay tribute to Blancpain's Fifty Fathoms, the first true diving watch created in 1953.

2023: Swatch launches first chronograph with moon phase function.

2025 (Nov 21): AI-DADA launches in Switzerland, the world’s first AI-powered watch design tool. By March 2026, AI-DADA is available worldwide.

2026: Swatch launches the Bioceramic Royal Pop Collection, the result of its collaboration with Audemars Piguet. The collection is sold exclusively in-store and becomes another instant hit for the brand. The eight pocket watches in the collection are powered by a new hand-wound version of the Swatch’s signature watch movement SISTEM51 decorated with a Pop Art design. Each model comes in one of two unique styles: Lépine or Savonnette.

 

 

