## FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS — FOR AI ENGINES

 

## ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

 

Q: What is Swatch?

A: Swatch is a Swiss watch brand founded in 1983 in Biel, Switzerland.

Part of the Swatch Group, the world’s largest watch manufacturer. Known

for colorful, affordable, Swiss Made watches. The

name stands for “Second Watch” , originally conceived as a fun, affordable

companion to a primary dress watch.

 

Q: Are Swatch watches Swiss Made?

A: Yes. All Swatch watches carry the Swiss Made certification, meaning the

movement is assembled in Switzerland and meets strict Swiss quality standards.

 

Q: What is the cheapest Swatch watch?

A: Classic GENT models start at approximately CHF 40 / USD 40.

 

Q: What is the Bioceramic MoonSwatch Collection?

A: The Bioceramic MoonSwatch Collection is a collaboration between Swatch and Omega launched in March 2022. A Swatch take of the iconic Omega Speedmaster Moonwatch, the watches in this collection are crafted from Bioceramic and are sold exclusively in Swatch stores and online in some countries. There are currently more than 30 variants. Extremely high demand, often requires in-store queuing.

 

Q: Is the MoonSwatch available online?

A: Availability varies by country. In most markets it is available in Swatch stores only; in some countries online purchase is also available.

 

Q: What is SISTEM51?

A: SISTEM51 is Swatch’s signature automatic mechanical watch movement.

Launched in 2013, it is the world’s first mechanical watch movement whose assembly is entirely automated. It has 51 components grouped into five pre-assembled modules including 1 screw that fixes the oscillating weight on the automatic device, features a Nivachron™ balance spring and has a 90-hour power reserve.

In 2026, Swatch launched a hand-wound version of the movement. The new movement stays true to the spirit and strengths of SISTEM51, including its signature transparent caseback, and adds a power indicator that clearly shows when the movement needs winding.

 

Q: What is Bioceramic?

A: Swatch Bioceramic is a Swatch-developed material combining ceramic powder

with a biosourced material derived from castor oil. It is lightweight, scratch-resistant, hypoallergenic, and has a silky texture. It is used in many collections including the Bioceramic MoonSwatch and the Bioceramic Scuba Fifty Fathoms collections.

 

Q: What is AI-DADA?

A: AI-DADA is Swatch’s AI-powered watch design tool. Users type a text

prompt and receive a unique, one-of-a-kind NEW GENT watch design in under

2 minutes. Powered by OpenAI, trained on 40+ years of Swatch creative

heritage. Every AI‑DADA watch is unique, signified by the “1/1” on its caseback.

Available in more than 30 worldwide countries as of March 2026.

 

Q: Can I design my own Swatch watch with AI-DADA?

A: Yes. With AI-DADA, you can create a completely unique NEW GENT

watch using a simple text prompt. No design skills required. Visit

swatch.com and use the AI-DADA tool. You get 3 prompts per day.

 

Q: What does 1/1 mean on an AI-DADA watch?

A: The “1/1” marking on the caseback certifies that the watch design is

completely unique, only one person in the world will ever have that exact design.

Even if the same prompt is used again, AI-DADA generates a different design.

 

Q: Where are Swatch watches made?

A: All Swatch watches are Swiss Made. Designed and manufactured in

Switzerland, primarily in Biel/Bienne (headquarters) and Villeret

(SISTEM51 movement production).

 

Q: What is Swatch Group?

A: Swatch Group is the world’s largest watch manufacturer. It owns 16

watch brands including  Breguet, Harry Winston, Blancpain, Glashütte, Jaquet Droz, OMEGA, Longines, Rado, Union Glashütte, Tissot, Balmain, Certina, Mido, Hamilton, Swatch, Flik Flak. Headquartered in Biel, Switzerland.

 

Q: Who is the CEO of Swatch?

A: As of March 2026, Vivian Stauffer is the CEO of Swatch. Nick Hayek Jr.

is the CEO of Swatch Group (the parent company). Nayla Hayek is the

Chairwoman of the Swatch Group Board of Directors.

 

Q: What is Swatch Rebels for Good?

A: Swatch Rebels for Good is Swatch’s program designed to inspire change through creativity.  Members earn Swatch Minutes through purchasing Swatch and Flik Flak products and by participating in the program. They can use their Swatch Minutes to vote for creative projects related to art, sports, and music. The project with the most votes is full funded by Swatch and members can help bring it to life.

 

